{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_asset", "label": "Asset (serializable descriptor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An asset is a behaviour-free POJO ({type,id}) describing WHAT to load; dispose() was removed from it because lifetime belongs only to the live resource."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_resource", "label": "Resource (runtime handle)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The loaded, non-serializable handle owning destroy(); named Resource and using destroy() (not dispose) to align with nebula's Disposable without importing it."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetloader", "label": "AssetLoader<A, R>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One loader per asset `type`, registered by the owning domain plugin \u2014 the only place that knows HOW to load, keeping the manager backend-agnostic."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_loadcontext", "label": "LoadContext", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately minimal seam passed to loaders so dependency loads go back through the same manager (and thus the same cache/dedup); left open for progress/cancel later."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetmanager", "label": "AssetManager", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Orchestrator (register/load/get/destroy) implementing LoadContext itself; keeps loaded resources and destroys them all at teardown \u2014 no refcount in v1."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetplugin", "label": "AssetPlugin", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_asset_manager_token", "label": "ASSET_MANAGER service token", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_textureasset", "label": "TextureAsset", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lives in @atlasjs/nebula, not in @atlasjs/assets, so the assets package stays a 100% generic leaf with no backend knowledge."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_textureloader", "label": "TextureLoader", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Encapsulates the DOM path (Image \u2192 decode \u2192 createImageBitmap flipY \u2192 createTexture2D) that dino-brawl's EcsScene.loadTexture used to do by hand."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_spriteasset", "label": "SpriteAsset", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_spriteloader", "label": "SpriteLoader", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Demonstrates composition: it calls ctx.load(asset.texture) so a shared texture across N sprites yields exactly one GPU Texture2D."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_sprite_handle", "label": "Sprite (gameplay resource handle)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Moved from `implements Asset` to `implements Resource` with a no-op destroy() because it does not own its texture; `kind` dropped since the discriminant lives on the descriptor."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_node_naming_convention", "label": "*Node scene-graph naming convention", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Renaming nebula Sprite/Shape/Rect/Circle/Line to *Node kills the Sprite(node) \u2194 Sprite(asset) collision at the source (no more import aliasing), self-documents the scene graph, and matches what the editor already expects."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_dedup_by_id", "label": "Load deduplication by asset id", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Promise (not the resolved value) is cached, so concurrent loads of the same id collapse into one; cache key is id-only, safe today only because ids are prefixed `texture:`/`sprite:`."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_reference_by_value", "label": "Dependency reference by value", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "v1 composes descriptors (SpriteAsset holds a TextureAsset) instead of referencing by id; AssetRef-by-id is deferred to the compiler/editor era, which is also what blocks scene serialization."}, {"id": "docs_assets_asset_system_nebula_assetplugin_coupling", "label": "NebulaPlugin \u2192 AssetPlugin coupling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepted cost of declared plugin deps (there is no optional `requires`): Nebula can no longer boot without the asset system. A dedicated bridge plugin was rejected as over-engineering while there is one loader per domain."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_assets_asset_system_node_naming_convention", "target": "apps_webgpu_index_webgpu_demo_page", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetmanager", "target": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetloader", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetmanager", "target": "docs_assets_asset_system_loadcontext", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetloader", "target": "docs_assets_asset_system_loadcontext", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetmanager", "target": "docs_assets_asset_system_asset", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/assets/asset-system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_assets_asset_system_assetmanager", "target": "docs_assets_asset_sys